   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Talking about plans",
     "texto": [
      "For plans in the near future, the **present** with a time word is very common: **Domani vado a Roma** (tomorrow I'm going to Rome), **Stasera guardo un film** (tonight I'm watching a film). **Andare a + infinitive** often expresses movement or intention to do something (**Vado a comprare il pane** = I'm going to buy bread); depending on context it can also refer to the near future, but it isn't the general equivalent of every future.",
      "Useful words: **domani** (tomorrow), **stasera** (tonight), **questo fine settimana**, **la settimana prossima** (next week). **Andare a trovare** means to visit someone."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Inviting and replying",
     "texto": [
      "**Vuoi venire?** (do you want to come?). More informal: **Ti va di venire?** (do you feel like coming?).",
      "To accept: **Volentieri!** (with pleasure!) or **Buona idea!** To decline: **Mi dispiace, non posso**. To agree or disagree: **Sono d'accordo** (I agree), **Non sono d'accordo** (I don't agree).",
      "To meet up: **Ci vediamo alle otto** (see you at eight)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
